 "notes": "COMPLETE. The 2026 General Election page (read in a real browser; curl gets a Cloudflare block) posts the county's 'Local Candidates for the November 3rd General Election' list plus sample ballots for all six precincts (Bayard, Casey, Guthrie Center, Panora, Stuart, Yale); all 6 PDFs (text layer) were parsed, covering every ballot style: Bayard, Seeley Twp, Union Twp, Casey, Baker Twp, Bear Grove Twp, Beaver Twp, Grant Twp, Guthrie Center, Jackson Twp, Valley Twp, Stuart, Beaver Twp, Diamondhead Sanitary, Panora, S. Panorama Sanitary (2 styles), Yale, Richland Twp, Seeley Twp. Supervisors are elected BY DISTRICT: District 1 (Phil Brown) on Bayard- and Casey-precinct styles, District 3 (Maggie Armstrong) on Panora-precinct styles, District 4 (Steve Smith) on Guthrie Center-precinct styles; Stuart and Yale precinct styles have no supervisor contest. Township contests: the candidate list says it covers all township offices on the ballot; townships not listed (e.g., Cass, Dodge, Highland, Orange, Penn, Thompson, Victory) have no township contest in 2026 and none appears on any sample ballot. Richland Township Trustee (vote for 2) and Clerk have no candidates filed (write-in only). Township name printed 'Seely Township' in contest titles (style header 'Seeley Township'). Jackson Twp Trustee is vote for one with two candidates. Diamondhead Sanitary District Trustee (vote for 2) has no candidates filed. Recorder name is printed 'Tristen Richard' on ballots ('Tristan' on the candidate list); ballot spelling kept. No county or local public measures on any of the six precincts' ballots (only statewide Amendment 1 and judicial retention)."
